[medium] The logic that auto-completes URL prefixes can get certain edge cases wrong:
1. A protocol-relative URL (e.g., '//example.com') ends up as 'https:////example.com'
2. A URL that already has another scheme (e.g., 'ftp://example.com') ends up as 'https://ftp://example.com'

A more robust check would be better, for example:
```java
if (!url.matches("^[a-zA-Z][a-zA-Z0-9+.-]*://.*")) {
    url = "https://" + url;
}
```
The regex accepts any valid protocol scheme, rather than only http/https.
